rota lap 4598, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; its cardinal seat is what-brix-infuse-is.md, whose claim is infusion(world') -> world', and whose instruction is to run the thing a second time
think Water tastes up close, so the lap looked for something to RUN twice rather than something to read. tools/c/convergence_census.sh is the tree's own reading of that claim, and it answered 14 candidates, 11 proven, 3 unproven.
think One of the three unproven was tools/fixtures/r/rish_spoken_ascii_convert.sh -- the converter I built last lap. I shipped a writer and never asked it the question this tree asks writers.
think The sibling prover invokes a tool as sh <tool> <one-path>, and the converter answers to --apply <path>..., so convergence_prove.sh cannot reach it. tools/c/convergence_tree_prove.sh takes <tool> [<arg>...] and runs it twice inside a throwaway git worktree, which is the shape this subject needs.
think Chose a subject that both converts and holds coupled sayings back, because the hold-back set is derived on every run rather than pinned -- a first run that changed the file could hand the second a different derivation, and that is where a second run would move if it moved anywhere.
think The first subject was tools/gen/chapter/prin_scope.rish, at three held lines the better sample, and naming it reddened tools/u/unheard_guard_witness.rish: unnamed_choirs fell 11 -> 10 because a path on a non-comment line reads as heard. My leg hands prin_scope to a converter AS A DATA FILE and never runs it, and that guard's first line is that a guard never run guards nothing. Moved the subject to tools/m/mycelium_chorus_knot_witness.rish and gave the fall back.
think No --perturb is owed, and that is the leg's own finding. Every prior subject runs in tools/hooks/pre-commit, so at HEAD its work is already done and a bare reading answers inert. This one is a sweep with 1,501 of 2,485 tracked .rish sources still holding a character it converts, so the committed tree is its own sample.
obs The whole sweep was proven too, off the roster: the same prover over all 2,485 tracked .rish paths at once reads verdict=converges. It stays out of the witness because its args= line alone runs 99KB, and a leg printing a hundred kilobytes of arguments teaches nothing. The one-file reading is what the witness carries.
obs A QA frame opened and closed on a number. The witness reads C+ 77 and read C+ 77 at HEAD, graded in a detached worktree at HEAD's bytes -- my leg moved neither figure. The whole gap is named_by_card=no, which this lap's card block repairs, and register=41 is a witness whose subject is refusal.
obs The red taught more than the leg did: a citation-as-data buys a ratchet fall in a guard whose whole subject is execution. Diagnosed by running the scan in a detached worktree at HEAD beside the working tree and diffing the forced choir listings, which named prin_scope as the single departure. Not booked, since the REDS pin is deadlocked at every row OPEN; named on the card instead, and it is unheard_guard's lane rather than mine.
obs index_row_bound read RED at the cold pass on rows_misordered=1 -- a peer's two rows out of stamp order on today's shelf, not mine. Closed with the repair its own advice names, sh tools/fixtures/i/index_shelf_repair.sh, which sorted 92 rows.
obs Two candidates stay unproven -- tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold.sh and tools/b/bootstrap_wasmtime.sh -- and neither is in my lane. reds_fold cannot be exercised while the REDS pin is deadlocked. Named on the card rather than taken.
